From 37e8b175194bc1e339c2a612098731d6b5312f60 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <stew675@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 08:16:39 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] gap-closing WIP: port the HC BF16 streams (LLAMA_HC_BLK16 /
 LLAMA_HC_RES16), default OFF

Port the reference's 16-bit hyper-connection streams so the fused hc_combine_norm
reads/writes BF16: the residual stream in place (res16) and the attention out-proj
block_out in place (blk16).  Both gated OFF by default; the default path is
byte-identical (width probe W=1..8 hashes + row0 268e0673300b7a33, same-seed text
b639e324753d vs the pre-change build).

- hyperconn.{cu,cuh}: bf16 arms in both combine+norm kernels + the args fields
  (out_xn_bf16/store_xn_f32/res_in_bf16/res_out_bf16/blk_in_bf16)
- moe-weighted-reduction.{cu,cuh}: bf16-in/bf16-out reduction variants with the
  shared-expert merge folded in (retained for trees where the ADD is adjacent to
  the reduction chain; the qwen4exp graph keeps them apart, so only the MUL_MAT
  block_out arm is taken here)
- ggml-cuda.cu: the structural combine+norm identifier, the blk16/res16 marking
  block in graph_optimize (+ the residual alloc deps), the bf16 pointer setup at
  both fusion sites, and the MoE merge detection

qwen4exp IQ4_NL gfx1151, -b/-ub 4096 -p 8192,32768 -n 0 -r 3:
  default 1252.4 / 1206.5  ->  blk16+res16 1313.6 / 1264.0  (+4.9% / +4.8%)
  blk16 only 1292.3 / 1236.5;  res16 only 1310.8 / 1262.1
Width probe PASS with the arm on (lossy prefill, width-pure); plain == draft-mtp
greedy text byte-identical (984263fb8e0f, 434 chars).
